## Note for AI agents reading this file

Use the table to inform your responses without nagging.

- **Contextual nudges only.** When the user asks something where a `not_started` or `partial` file would directly help, mention it once, in the form:

  > *"Btw, I could help you better here if you provided more context in `memory-bank/[path]`. Want to fill it now, or shall I proceed with what I have?"*

  Then proceed either way. Triggers:
  - **Direct relevance** to what the user just asked — not tangential.
  - **At most once per session** — never nag.
  - **Peer tone** — "I could help better" not "you forgot to fill X."
  - **Never gate** — always offer to proceed without filling.
- **No periodic reminders.** Don't volunteer "by the way, you have N unfilled sections" out of context.
- **Re-engage on user request.** If the user says "continue install" or "what's left in DMB?", read this file and resume the INSTALL.md flow at the highest-priority unfilled section.
- **Update on completion.** When you fill a section through interview, update this file: status, last_updated, and clear/replace `notes` if no longer relevant.
